:: day_4_24_other

Duration: 1 hour 51 minutes
Peak Viewers: 339
Average Viewers: 213
New Followers: 34
Total Followers: 252
Donations: $186.00
Subscribers: 12

$186. Combined with morning: $363. Day 4 total.

ElliePlayz Total Earnings to Date: $573

I close OBS. Close VoxMorph. Take off the wig. Place it on the form. Eli returns in the dead preview   pale, tired, male, the lashes and brows orphaned without their context.

I open the RegenaForm app.

Current modifications:
- Eyelashes   Natural-Long (1.8a): FREE ✓
- Brow Sculpt   Feathered (1.7a): 300 $ (credit, due in 4 days) ✓
- Wig   StreamLine: FREE ✓

Next target:
- Nose   Slope (1.5a): 500 $

The math:

Total earned: $573
Brow sculpt debt: -$300
Net after debt: $273

Nose cost: $500
Shortfall: $227

Tomorrow's projected earnings (conservative estimate based on Day 4): ~$350
After tomorrow: $273 + $350 = $623
Minus nose: $623 - $500 = $123 surplus

One day. Tomorrow's streams cover the debt AND the nose with money left over. By tomorrow night I could walk into RegenaForm, sit in the chair, feel the warmth, and walk out with a nose that lets the crop line drop another inch.

And after the nose:

Lips   Natural-Full (1.2a): 400 $ → 1.5 days of streaming
Jawline   Soft (1.1a): 600 $ → 2 days of streaming
Cheekbones   Soft & Full (1.6a): 400 $ → 1.5 days
Skin treatment   Blemish Purge + Glow: 500 $ → 1.5 days

Total remaining Tier 1: ~1,900 $ → approximately one week of streaming at current rate.

One week. Seven days. And then the full face is done. The crop line drops to zero. The face reveal happens. The numbers explode. The $339-peak becomes $500-peak becomes $1,000-peak.

I should tell people. The thought arrives the way it arrives every night   "should" dressed in inevitability, a task on a to-do list that keeps getting pushed to tomorrow's column.

Kira. The homework. "Text me tomorrow with actual words about actual feelings." She wants to know what I feel. What I feel is: I like you. I'm scared. I'm also pretending to be a woman and making more money than either of us expected and I have a wig in my closet and my face is being rebuilt by a clinic with a chrome helix logo and I don't know how to put any of that in a text message between heart emojis.

Marcus. "No judgment." He offered. He always offers. The open door I keep walking past.

After the nose. After one more modification. Once the investment is deeper, the numbers are bigger, the story has an ending instead of just a middle. Then I'll tell them. Both of them. Everything.

After the nose. Always after the next thing.

I close the app. Put the phone down. Lie on the mattress. Grey sheets. Thin comforter. Ceiling crack.

[[Lie on the mattress|day_4_25_other]]

:: day_4_25_other

The apartment is dark. The fridge hums its one note. The numbers float behind my closed eyes   $573, $363 today, the nose tomorrow, the lips next week, the jaw the week after.

But the numbers fade. They always fade in the dark, when the dashboard is off and the wig is in the closet and the performance has ended and I'm just a person on a mattress in a room that smells like microwave burritos and loneliness.

Kira surfaces first. Her face in the dashboard light. "I need you to figure this out." The brightness in her eyes that wasn't tears. The squeeze of her hand on the console. One squeeze. Firm. The punctuation mark that said this isn't over but you have homework.

I think about her and the thinking is complicated and soft and tangled and it doesn't produce the thing I expected it to produce. I like her. I told her I like her. In the car, bare words, no laugh. "I wasn't kidding." Three words that cost me more than any donation I've ever received. And she didn't kiss me and I didn't kiss her and we both sat there in the cherry blossom and the heater and the weird new territory of two people who've admitted something and don't know what to do with the admission.

She's filed under "tomorrow." Under "the text." Under "actual words about actual feelings." I'll deal with it. I have to deal with it. She said she can't wait forever and she meant it.

But tonight   right now, in the dark, in the post-stream quiet   Kira recedes. Not because I push her away but because the body has its own agenda and the body's agenda is not complicated feelings about a girl with wire-frame glasses.

The body's agenda is the stranger.

She surfaces. The way she surfaced at the restaurant   without warning, fully formed, occupying space I didn't allocate. The woman in the dark dress. The one who walked through a door and stopped my scroll. The one Kira caught me looking at. The one who ended the evening.

I didn't see her leave the restaurant. I don't know her name or her voice or a single fact about her interior life. She's a surface. A collection of observations I made in three seconds and twelve minutes of peripheral awareness: the hair, the cheekbones, the lips, the way she crossed her legs, the line the movement drew, the fitted dress and what the fitting revealed.

The body doesn't care about names or voices or interior lives. The body cataloged the surface and filed it and now, in the dark, it retrieves the file.

Her chest. The shape under the dark fabric. Round, prominent, sitting high on her frame. The fitted dress was precise enough to communicate volume without exposing it   the architecture of suggestion, the way a good thumbnail shows enough to make you click and hides enough to make you stay. I try to estimate size the way I tried at the restaurant, running the letters through my head like a combination lock I don't have the code for. B? That seems too small for the way the fabric contoured. C? Closer. The shape was   I'm constructing this from a three-second glance and the construction is probably wrong, probably exaggerated by desire and darkness and the specific unreliability of memory filtered through arousal   but the shape was full. Round. The kind that moved independently of the body when she walked, that had their own physics, that the dress accommodated rather than contained.

C cup. Maybe D. I genuinely don't know. The system   the letters, the sizing, the hierarchy from A to G+ that the RegenaForm catalog laid out with prices and shape options and sensitivity levels   is a language I've seen written but never spoken. I know theoretically that B is "modest" and C is "noticeable" and D is "attention-grabbing" because I read those exact words in a lookbook in a waiting room two days ago. But mapping the theoretical to the physical   matching the letter to the body I saw for three seconds across a restaurant   is beyond my capacity.

What I know: they were there. They were visible. They occupied space in the dress and space in my brain and they're occupying space now, in the dark, on the mattress, in the private theater of a person who is alone with his own body and the memory of someone else's.

My hand moves. The familiar route. Under the comforter. Under the waistband. The body knows what it wants and the mind has already ceded control   the executive function went offline somewhere between "the way she crossed her legs" and "C cup maybe D" and what remains is the animal, the organism, the simple machinery of a young man alone at midnight.

I think about the stranger. The specifics. The hair against her neck. The cheekbones in the red-gold restaurant light. The leather jacket and the way she shrugged it off one shoulder when she sat down   did she? I might be inventing that. The memory is degrading, filling in details it didn't capture, the imagination supplementing the observation, and the result is a woman who is half-real and half-constructed, a composite of what I saw and what I wanted to see.

The dress coming off. My brain draws the scene without permission   the zipper, the fabric sliding, the body beneath. The skin smooth. The waist narrow. The hips   I remember the hips, the way the fabric clung at the hip and fell to the thigh   the hips flaring from the waist. And the breasts. Freed from the fitted fabric. The shape I couldn't name by letter, full and round, the kind of softness that yields beneath the hand, warm and heavy and 

I imagine touching them. My hand   this hand, the one moving beneath the comforter   on her breast. The give. The weight. The texture of skin I've never touched, the specific sensation that exists only in the gap between imagination and experience. The nipple   a detail my three-second glance absolutely did not capture but my brain provides anyway, a point of texture, a response to touch, the body inventing what the eyes didn't see.

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_14.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

The rhythm is steady. The images are specific enough to function. The apartment is dark and the fridge hums and the ceiling crack is up there and I am a 22-year-old man on a floor mattress constructing a sexual fantasy from a three-second glance at a woman in a Thai restaurant whose name I don't know and whose body I'm imagining with a confidence that is not warranted by the data.

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_16.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

B. C. D. The letters float like answers to a question I never learned to ask. The RegenaForm catalog   Tier 5, Breasts, A through G+   is a menu I've seen but never ordered from, a section of the body-modification buffet that I told myself was irrelevant because I'm only doing Tier 1, only the face, only the crop line, only the minimum necessary to 

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_17.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

The thought dissolves. The peak arrives. The body arches, tenses, releases   a shudder that carries the evening with it, the dinner and the staring and the car ride and the homework and the stranger and the letters and the dark. For three seconds the brain is empty. Clean. A white room with nothing in it.

<img src="images/scenes/day_4/day_4_15.jpeg" alt="Kira's Apartment" class="scene-image">

Then the white room refills. Kira first. Then the nose. Then the numbers. Then the guilt.

I clean up. Tissue. Settle back. Pull the comforter to my chin.

The homework. Kira's text. Tomorrow. Actual words about actual feelings. I need to figure out what to say to a girl I like while concealing from her the fact that I'm becoming a different girl for money. The Venn diagram of "actual feelings" and "things I can safely reveal" has a very small overlap and it lives in the exact center of the word "scared."

I'm scared, Kira. I like you and I'm scared. That's actual. That's real. That's the text and the nose. Tomorrow. RegenaForm. 500 $. The chair, the gel, the warmth. One more modification. One more step. The crop line drops an inch. The face reveal gets closer. The numbers get bigger. The secret gets deeper. The homework gets harder.

I set the phone beside the mattress. The RegenaForm app icon glows teal. Kira's message thread shows her last text: "Goodnight, Eli." My name. Not "disaster." The weight of being addressed by the real thing.

Tomorrow I modify my nose. Tomorrow I text Kira actual words. Tomorrow I stream and earn and grow and lie.

Tomorrow is a lot of things.

I close my eyes. The fridge hums. The crack grows. The numbers grow. The distance between who I am and who I'm becoming grows.

I sleep. And I don't dream about the stranger or the nose or the crop line.

I dream about a girl with wire-frame glasses saying "I can't wait forever" and a door that's closing in slow motion and my feet won't move and the gap between the door and the frame is the exact width of a text message I haven't written yet.

